WEBVTT

00:00.980 --> 00:04.350
Keep Out!!

00:20.650 --> 00:22.910
I don't see how this could lure him out.

00:23.180 --> 00:26.220
No, Senpai has locked himself in his room

00:26.220 --> 00:29.250
for the past two weeks,
hardly eating or drinking.

00:29.660 --> 00:31.630
Surely his favorite food will work.

00:31.860 --> 00:33.720
Maybe he's already dead.

00:33.720 --> 00:35.510
That's uncalled for!

00:35.990 --> 00:39.390
He's right though.
The last time I saw him...

00:39.850 --> 00:42.900
No, this if when my has is what by...

00:48.530 --> 00:50.770
I <i>am</i> a little worried.

00:51.250 --> 00:53.470
And this is an opportunity.

00:53.800 --> 00:56.210
If I can get him to approve of my piece...

00:56.210 --> 00:58.200
Your piece? It's just a gyoza
recipe you ripped off.

00:58.200 --> 00:59.970
It's not a rip-off!

00:59.970 --> 01:01.600
It's in no way an imitation!

01:04.310 --> 01:06.880
It's a howl of joy.

01:08.010 --> 01:11.500
He must have been pleased with my gyoza.

01:14.170 --> 01:15.850
Senpai...

01:23.630 --> 01:25.980
Wrong!

02:56.900 --> 03:01.360
09: "Beyond the Darkness"

03:00.200 --> 03:02.780
He looks legit pissed.

03:03.100 --> 03:06.450
He must have really hated Schu-kun's gyoza.

03:06.450 --> 03:07.370
Wrong!

03:07.770 --> 03:09.680
Wrong, wrong!

03:10.130 --> 03:11.210
Wrong!

03:11.210 --> 03:15.200
I really don't care, but would
you please not destroy the room?

03:16.460 --> 03:19.380
Damn it, you've made such a mess.

03:19.640 --> 03:20.590
What? What?

03:20.590 --> 03:22.130
What've you been doing, Lud-kun?

03:25.390 --> 03:28.360
Were you making a guitar?

03:28.660 --> 03:30.310
You can <i>make</i> guitars?

03:30.830 --> 03:34.060
There's no instrument that
wasn't handmade at first.

03:34.510 --> 03:36.700
But why is Beethes-san doing that?

03:37.680 --> 03:39.570
I wanted to play.

03:40.300 --> 03:43.000
It was two weeks ago...

04:07.580 --> 04:10.050
So you decided you want to play.

04:10.800 --> 04:12.950
You didn't have to make
one yourself, though.

04:12.950 --> 04:14.420
No!

04:14.420 --> 04:16.920
An ideal performance requires
an ideal instrument.

04:16.920 --> 04:19.540
The sound I seek cannot be created

04:19.540 --> 04:21.970
by just any ordinary instrument.

04:21.970 --> 04:24.910
So that's why you've been a hermit lately.

04:24.910 --> 04:27.810
But I can't get it to sound how I want.

04:28.110 --> 04:30.930
I know exactly what I want,

04:30.930 --> 04:33.750
but it refuses to appear before me.

04:34.010 --> 04:36.880
Hey, are you not making gyoza anymore?

04:36.880 --> 04:37.850
Gyoza?

04:37.850 --> 04:38.670
What is that?

04:38.670 --> 04:39.530
What?!

04:39.530 --> 04:41.880
After all that fuss you made?

04:44.130 --> 04:47.250
Wh-Why are you laughing all of a sudden?

04:47.250 --> 04:49.490
You would never understand, commoner.

04:49.490 --> 04:52.060
This joy, this glory...

04:52.490 --> 04:54.450
Senpai is going to play the guitar.

04:54.900 --> 04:58.480
This means we get to hear

04:58.480 --> 05:01.480
the great Beethoven's performance live!

05:02.160 --> 05:03.670
Oh, yeah!

05:07.380 --> 05:09.550
Beethes-san's going to play,

05:09.550 --> 05:11.870
which means he's going to do Musik.

05:11.870 --> 05:14.740
I'm going to play along, and...

05:18.200 --> 05:19.880
Thank you, thank you.

05:23.100 --> 05:24.060
Thank you.

05:24.060 --> 05:25.800
What's with the cruddy guitar?

05:25.800 --> 05:27.600
It's not cruddy!

05:27.900 --> 05:31.060
I'm kind of a musician, too, you know.

05:31.390 --> 05:33.050
It doesn't take anything to <i>say</i> you are.

05:33.050 --> 05:36.230
So, what does this kind-of-a-musician want?

05:36.600 --> 05:39.680
I thought I'd help Beethes-san
make his guitar.

05:39.680 --> 05:40.890
You, Sousuke?

05:40.890 --> 05:41.690
Yeah.

05:41.690 --> 05:45.940
And I'll have him teach
me how to do Musik, and...

05:46.360 --> 05:48.550
Musik!

05:52.800 --> 05:54.240
Why are you giggling?

05:54.780 --> 05:59.420
He's probably fantasizing about using
Musik and having girls fuss over him.

05:59.420 --> 06:01.000
How did you know?!

06:01.420 --> 06:02.640
I see.

06:02.640 --> 06:03.510
So shallow.

06:03.510 --> 06:05.020
Hey, Beethes-san.

06:06.370 --> 06:09.150
Senpai is exhausted from his creative work.

06:09.450 --> 06:11.220
Please don't talk to him
if you have no reason to.

06:11.490 --> 06:14.830
But here, have it. As a reference
for your guitar making.

06:14.830 --> 06:17.890
I thought it might help you along if
you had something to work off of.

06:27.670 --> 06:29.250
Wanna do a song?

06:31.520 --> 06:32.560
What's the matter?

06:32.560 --> 06:34.100
How do you play?

06:35.240 --> 06:38.420
Wait, don't tell me you
can't play at all, Beethes.

06:38.760 --> 06:39.730
Of course not.

06:39.730 --> 06:42.090
Then what's the point of having a guitar?

06:42.090 --> 06:44.190
I want to play, so I want to play!

06:44.190 --> 06:45.630
You aren't a kid.

06:46.940 --> 06:49.180
Then why don't I, Sousuke-san,

06:49.180 --> 06:52.250
show you the ropes of guitar myself?

06:52.250 --> 06:55.510
Wh— How could you be so
condescending to Senpai?!

06:55.860 --> 06:58.120
That's pretty bold, tool.

06:58.120 --> 07:02.020
He's on his high horse because he's
better at something for once.

07:02.310 --> 07:04.790
Shush, we don't need backseat drivers.

07:05.090 --> 07:07.630
What matters is how Beethes-san feels.

07:07.630 --> 07:08.460
Well?

07:08.760 --> 07:11.240
I'll do anything, if it's for my music.

07:11.540 --> 07:13.950
Good. I like your attitude.

07:13.950 --> 07:16.670
Even if that means seeking help

07:16.670 --> 07:18.760
from a foolish beginner.

07:18.760 --> 07:20.960
You didn't need to say that.

07:21.250 --> 07:22.130
Good.

07:22.130 --> 07:24.100
Let's begin our lesson.

07:24.100 --> 07:25.650
Come with me, boy!

07:25.650 --> 07:28.210
I'm the one teaching you, you know.

07:28.210 --> 07:31.050
Basic Guitar Technique

07:50.370 --> 07:51.360
Wh-What?!

07:51.360 --> 07:52.460
No!

07:52.460 --> 07:53.800
This is all wrong!

07:53.800 --> 07:55.500
Wait, that's my guitar.

07:55.500 --> 07:57.370
I can't create an ideal sound with this.

07:57.370 --> 08:01.190
I told you, this is just a reference
for your guitar making.

08:01.190 --> 08:02.790
You'll find your ideal guitar.

08:03.050 --> 08:05.670
No. I'm borrowing that for a while.

08:06.680 --> 08:09.440
I'm going to turn it into
the ideal instrument.

08:09.440 --> 08:12.170
For an ideal sound! An ideal performance!

08:12.450 --> 08:15.020
Wait, Beethes, aren't you a composer?

08:15.020 --> 08:17.550
Why are you so bent on performing?

08:18.560 --> 08:20.190
Something is restless within me...

08:21.170 --> 08:23.000
When I think about performing,

08:23.000 --> 08:25.700
it awakens something restless within me.

08:26.060 --> 08:28.150
I want to find out what that something is.

08:28.390 --> 08:29.470
Something? What?

08:29.470 --> 08:31.360
This would be so much easier
if I knew what it was!

08:31.360 --> 08:32.960
Oh, right.

08:33.300 --> 08:34.110
But...

08:34.520 --> 08:35.410
But?

08:35.660 --> 08:37.830
When I try to think about it,

08:38.220 --> 08:40.840
I become strangely sentimental.

08:43.330 --> 08:45.910
Now, I'm borrowing this.

08:49.700 --> 08:52.070
There's no way that piece of junk

08:52.070 --> 08:54.550
would be adequate for Senpai's dreams.

08:54.860 --> 08:58.650
I need the ultimate guitar,
befitting of Senpai.

08:59.610 --> 09:03.030
But how would I acquire it?

09:03.370 --> 09:05.800
What can I do?

09:07.890 --> 09:10.090
Hey, aren't you making your guitar?

09:10.090 --> 09:13.540
I've decided that I should return
to where it all started first.

09:16.840 --> 09:20.780
I want to become a huge
artist that gets plastered

09:20.780 --> 09:23.210
on huge screens like that someday.

09:23.750 --> 09:26.960
I'm challenged to a solo stage

09:30.770 --> 09:38.930
A world of my imagination comes into motion

09:40.250 --> 09:42.130
Street performers.

09:42.130 --> 09:44.790
I'm really not interested
in boring stuff like this.

09:42.570 --> 09:49.210
Cast magic on the melody
playing in the night

09:51.170 --> 09:54.800
It looks like Beethes-san
shut himself in again.

09:54.800 --> 09:56.820
I wonder if he's making any progress.

09:57.890 --> 09:59.910
'Sup. Are you at it?

10:00.200 --> 10:01.940
You've come at a good time.

10:01.940 --> 10:05.030
I just finished tuning your guitar.

10:05.560 --> 10:07.160
What the hell?!

10:07.460 --> 10:11.450
I've taken the liberty of tinkering with
it a little, to produce the ideal sound.

10:12.720 --> 10:13.930
Behold!

10:15.870 --> 10:18.260
Does it not set your soul on fire?

10:20.990 --> 10:22.640
My guitar...

10:22.720 --> 10:34.360
Firepower!!

10:22.870 --> 10:24.590
I call it Monster!

10:24.590 --> 10:27.630
It's far from the ideal sound that I pursue,

10:27.630 --> 10:30.780
but it's more than enough
to get me riled up.

10:30.780 --> 10:34.360
With this here Monster,
I shall find the ideal sound!

10:38.890 --> 10:40.990
It's smoking!

10:52.460 --> 10:54.850
Dude, this is bad!

10:54.850 --> 10:56.670
It's pitch black!
What the heck happened?

10:56.670 --> 10:59.410
Please, it's too dark. I can't see.

11:03.350 --> 11:04.440
I can't hear.

11:05.430 --> 11:06.260
Anything.

11:07.150 --> 11:09.200
My music life...

11:10.040 --> 11:10.880
is...

11:15.690 --> 11:18.240
What have you gone and done this time?

11:18.570 --> 11:19.900
It's probably this.

11:20.820 --> 11:22.000
A guitar?

11:22.000 --> 11:24.300
I think it uses a ton of power.

11:24.300 --> 11:24.910
What?

11:25.260 --> 11:28.250
Damn it. It's pitch black, thanks to you.

11:29.600 --> 11:31.820
Hey, Beethes, are you listening?

11:32.210 --> 11:34.770
I said, "It's pitch black, thanks to you."

11:34.770 --> 11:36.930
Ah, how's this, then?

11:38.100 --> 11:39.670
That's not the point!

11:40.170 --> 11:43.510
Listen, as the landlady,
I'm going to give you an order.

11:43.510 --> 11:46.970
From now on, you may not play any instruments

11:47.290 --> 11:49.220
that'll cause trouble for the others.

12:03.730 --> 12:07.120
I mean, yeah, I haven't touched
that guitar in a while,

12:09.370 --> 12:11.510
but that's just way too much.

12:14.420 --> 12:17.920
Guitar Contest!!
Grand Prize: Croquis

12:15.220 --> 12:17.600
Guitar contest?

12:18.150 --> 12:21.440
"The winner receives a Croquis"?

12:22.450 --> 12:25.680
"Electric guitar Croquis"...

12:25.680 --> 12:27.470
Search

12:26.040 --> 12:27.780
Search results...

12:27.780 --> 12:30.160
It looks to be quite a premium guitar.

12:30.160 --> 12:32.350
It may be too good for you.

12:32.350 --> 12:33.800
Shut up!

12:34.470 --> 12:38.190
Retail price, one, ten, hundred...

12:40.670 --> 12:42.830
All right!

12:50.330 --> 12:51.490
I can't hear.

12:53.040 --> 12:53.810
Anything.

12:55.470 --> 12:57.950
Just what was that?

12:59.940 --> 13:03.810
Say, maybe you went too far,
banning him from playing.

13:03.810 --> 13:05.150
It's fine.

13:05.150 --> 13:06.930
He needs that much.

13:07.450 --> 13:08.450
Beethes-san.

13:08.450 --> 13:11.010
It's no good. He's still frozen.

13:12.050 --> 13:14.140
Hey, Beethes-san, forget that...

13:14.140 --> 13:15.810
Just what was that?!

13:16.950 --> 13:18.500
Did you need something, boy?

13:18.500 --> 13:20.800
Don't "Did you need something" me.

13:20.800 --> 13:23.190
Hey, so anyway, take a look at this.

13:24.700 --> 13:27.120
And that's why you're a brilliant musician.

13:27.120 --> 13:29.210
You know when you're looking
at something good.

13:29.210 --> 13:31.010
This is the Croquis.

13:31.010 --> 13:32.990
It's a super-famous, super-rare...

13:32.830 --> 13:33.870
Guitar Contest!!
Grand prize: Croquis

13:33.870 --> 13:36.940
This may be my ideal guitar.

13:37.240 --> 13:38.970
Don't you want to play it?

13:38.970 --> 13:39.630
Indeed!

13:39.940 --> 13:43.950
There's a good way to make it ours.

13:52.460 --> 13:53.810
Wait, wait.

13:53.810 --> 13:56.450
No one said you could perform.

13:56.450 --> 13:58.320
We know.

13:58.320 --> 14:02.300
That's why we're modding this so
we can use it at the contest.

14:02.300 --> 14:04.620
Are you seriously going
to make Beethes play?

14:04.620 --> 14:05.490
Of course.

14:05.960 --> 14:09.010
In exchange for my guitar...

14:09.010 --> 14:10.930
Yes. The prize guitar.

14:10.930 --> 14:13.870
I just need to perform with it,
and then I'll give it to the boy.

14:14.200 --> 14:16.780
Why are you assuming you're going to win?

14:16.780 --> 14:18.150
This sounds fun.

14:18.150 --> 14:19.500
Let me in.

14:19.500 --> 14:21.950
You're more than welcome.

14:21.950 --> 14:23.610
Modding sounds fun.

14:23.610 --> 14:24.920
It's love, Cho-chan.

14:24.920 --> 14:27.130
Thanks, everyone.

14:31.670 --> 14:35.470
Beethoven registered for the guitar contest.

14:36.150 --> 14:38.970
We were saying it's weird that he'd come,

14:38.970 --> 14:40.690
knowing we're hosting it.

14:41.300 --> 14:42.550
What do we do?

14:49.190 --> 14:50.300
What's wrong?

14:50.300 --> 14:52.860
I think it's pretty sweet.

14:52.860 --> 14:53.770
What is this?

14:53.770 --> 14:55.610
What is this thing?

14:56.510 --> 15:00.000
I tried incorporating
everyone's opinions, and...

15:00.000 --> 15:01.400
I don't understand!

15:01.400 --> 15:03.070
Calm down.

15:03.070 --> 15:04.160
What is this?

15:04.470 --> 15:08.060
This pain-like anxiousness
gutting the depths of my soul?

15:09.520 --> 15:12.130
I'm too distracted to focus
on building the guitar!

15:12.130 --> 15:14.010
You weren't talking about
building the guitar?

15:14.010 --> 15:14.980
I don't know.

15:14.980 --> 15:16.520
I don't know. I don't know!

15:16.820 --> 15:19.580
Just where is this sentimentality

15:19.580 --> 15:22.430
coming at me from?

15:23.360 --> 15:24.380
Lud-kun.

15:24.380 --> 15:25.530
Where are you going?

15:25.530 --> 15:26.440
I don't know.

15:27.630 --> 15:29.880
What's gotten into him?

15:34.260 --> 15:37.770
What is this something<i> that I seek?</i>

15:39.040 --> 15:43.680
And what is this anxiousness
gutting the depths of my soul?

15:48.050 --> 15:49.110
I can't see.

15:49.680 --> 15:52.700
I can't see anything right now.

16:02.730 --> 16:09.500
Cast magic on the melody
playing in the night

16:09.500 --> 16:11.270
Neither her song nor

16:11.270 --> 16:13.630
her singing is particularly noteworthy.

16:12.100 --> 16:20.140
You're going to shine
brighter than the stars

16:14.120 --> 16:16.470
So why am I so...

16:20.140 --> 16:23.680
Believe you can make it happen

16:36.930 --> 16:39.060
Contestant
Waiting Room C

16:38.240 --> 16:40.460
Beethoven's still not here.

16:40.460 --> 16:41.410
Damn it.

16:41.410 --> 16:45.020
What's the point of entering
if he gets disqualified?

16:46.890 --> 16:47.770
Is he back?

16:48.050 --> 16:49.070
No.

16:49.070 --> 16:50.740
He hasn't come home since yesterday night.

16:51.190 --> 16:53.950
I thought he might come straight here.

16:54.250 --> 16:57.240
Number 28, stand by, please.

16:57.240 --> 16:59.040
That's Beethes-san!

16:59.040 --> 17:00.280
Is he not here?

17:00.280 --> 17:01.970
If he's not here, I'll write
him down as dropped out.

17:01.970 --> 17:03.380
No, no!

17:03.380 --> 17:04.620
Are you Number 28?

17:04.620 --> 17:07.250
No, I'm just here with him.

17:07.250 --> 17:08.650
Then where is he?

17:08.650 --> 17:10.450
Well, I...

17:10.450 --> 17:11.730
I'm right here.

17:13.190 --> 17:14.550
Beethes-san!

17:14.550 --> 17:15.720
Damn it.

17:15.720 --> 17:17.630
Please be ready, now that you're here.

17:17.630 --> 17:20.310
I was so worried.

17:23.860 --> 17:25.060
I'm going to focus.

17:25.560 --> 17:26.830
Let me be alone.

17:29.860 --> 17:32.860
Next, Number 28.

17:39.030 --> 17:40.500
What's up with the guitar?

17:40.500 --> 17:41.230
Weak.

17:41.230 --> 17:42.540
Is he going to be okay with that thing?

17:59.420 --> 18:00.650
What the heck?

18:00.650 --> 18:01.640
A blackout?

18:02.970 --> 18:05.070
Dude, what's going on?

18:05.070 --> 18:07.230
You can't play without power, right?

18:23.270 --> 18:24.380
I can't hear.

18:25.330 --> 18:26.340
Anything.

18:27.420 --> 18:29.200
I can't hear anything with my ears.

18:30.810 --> 18:32.600
Is this my fate?

18:35.120 --> 18:37.350
My future is far in the darkness.

18:41.420 --> 18:42.680
The darkness.

18:52.350 --> 18:53.130
No.

18:53.910 --> 18:54.870
Not yet.

18:55.850 --> 18:57.830
I may not be able to play,

18:57.830 --> 19:00.660
but I can still write a piece
and present it to the world.

19:01.810 --> 19:05.440
I must break new ground as a composer.

19:06.550 --> 19:09.110
I must abandon the glory
of being a performer.

19:18.650 --> 19:20.800
The <i>something</i> stirring within me...

19:21.110 --> 19:24.210
The anxiousness in my soul is the future

19:24.210 --> 19:27.550
I buried deep within the darkness.

19:29.890 --> 19:35.850
Spielen wir unsere Musik!

19:50.050 --> 19:51.120
Isn't this...

19:51.120 --> 19:52.920
Here we go, Musik!

19:53.190 --> 19:55.540
I am guided to my new path

19:55.890 --> 19:57.760
by my spirit!

19:59.520 --> 20:01.340
Come on, baby!

20:03.280 --> 20:07.180
A lone star in the dark night

20:07.180 --> 20:11.050
A faint light it may be

20:11.050 --> 20:14.770
But it shows the way to tomorrow

20:15.680 --> 20:21.780
Now, open, door to the future

20:18.440 --> 20:21.460
Violin Sonata No. 9, "Kreutzer."

20:22.350 --> 20:26.100
One of the pieces Beethoven
completed as a student when he

20:22.500 --> 20:26.340
Escape from the jail of despair

20:25.530 --> 20:29.290
Ludwig van Beethoven

20:26.100 --> 20:28.500
first abandoned his pursuit
of becoming a performer,

20:27.320 --> 20:30.150
I am reborn

20:28.500 --> 20:30.750
and switched fully into composition.

20:31.120 --> 20:35.220
Let sing this six-stringed weapon

20:35.220 --> 20:41.130
The world cowers before me, the monster

20:36.470 --> 20:37.660
Beethes-san...

20:42.640 --> 20:46.570
A lone star in the dark night

20:43.260 --> 20:45.530
With this melody,

20:45.530 --> 20:48.850
I will wrench open the darkness
and cut through the silence.

20:46.570 --> 20:50.600
A faint light it may be

20:49.960 --> 20:53.300
My sword of resistance was

20:50.600 --> 20:55.400
But it shows the way to tomorrow

20:53.760 --> 20:55.560
in my hands all along.

21:03.820 --> 21:07.620
There is light here in my heart

21:10.720 --> 21:12.160
Hey, Beethes-san...

21:13.380 --> 21:15.290
Well, I mean, y'know,

21:15.590 --> 21:19.100
even with everything that happened,
you ended up a huge composer.

21:19.100 --> 21:20.090
I'm glad for you.

21:20.560 --> 21:24.500
All's well that ends well in life, right?

21:25.110 --> 21:27.250
Whose life are you saying has ended?

21:29.100 --> 21:30.330
The past is the past.

21:30.680 --> 21:31.870
Now is now.

21:32.670 --> 21:35.310
I'm still newly born.

21:38.760 --> 21:41.150
It isn't bothering him one bit anymore.

21:44.300 --> 21:46.170
C-Can I help you?

21:46.730 --> 21:49.840
Your devotion has shown me to the light.

21:50.370 --> 21:51.550
This is a gift as thanks.

21:54.870 --> 21:55.990
This isn't...

21:56.360 --> 21:57.850
H-Hey!

21:57.850 --> 21:59.840
You said you'd give me the prize guitar!

22:02.380 --> 22:05.090
I don't know what to do with
this weird-ass guitar.

22:05.090 --> 22:08.510
It's not instruments or technique
that you need for music.

22:09.880 --> 22:11.080
I see.

22:11.450 --> 22:13.310
It's talent, isn't it?

22:15.810 --> 22:16.560
Hot, hot!

22:18.400 --> 22:19.060
Senpai.

22:22.630 --> 22:26.180
An ideal guitar calls for
high-quality materials.

22:26.180 --> 22:29.020
I, Schubert, went to Cuba.

22:29.020 --> 22:31.960
Now you can use an ideal guitar
to play in an ideal performance.

22:31.960 --> 22:33.860
The performance is finished.

24:15.970 --> 24:27.400
"Jolly Love"

24:16.320 --> 24:18.140
Chopin, Cho-chan, and Mr. Recluse.

24:18.140 --> 24:20.020
Cry not, grieve not, for it is fate.

24:20.020 --> 24:21.560
Life is nothing but farewells.

24:21.560 --> 24:23.210
There is as much love as there are goodbyes.

24:23.210 --> 24:24.650
There are as many songs
as there are goodbyes.

24:24.650 --> 24:26.690
Speak of the Musik of parting.

24:26.690 --> 24:28.950
Let resound the Musik of love.
